<title>POLAND: Polish city of Jaslo to issue muni bonds in 1997.</title>
<headline>Polish city of Jaslo to issue muni bonds in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The southern Polish town of Jaslo plans to issue two million zlotys worth of municipal bonds next year to finance the modernisation of its sewage and water systems, the mayor said.</p>
<p>PAP news agency reported Janusz Rak as saying the sale of the one- or two-year paper was likely in the middle of next year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
